  <section id="research" class="academic-section" aria-labelledby="research-title">
    <h2 id="research-title">Research</h2>
    <p>I study how large generative models can become persistent and interactive world simulators. My current work connects three problems:</p>
    <ul class="research-directions">
      <li><strong>World-Action Models:</strong> predicting future visual states conditioned on user or agent actions.</li>
      <li><strong>Persistent spatial memory:</strong> retaining map-level context beyond a short video window.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Multi-view world consistency:</strong> maintaining a stable shared world under rapid motion, viewpoint changes, and long rollouts.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

